<title>USA: Global Industrial unit wins contract.</title>
<headline>Global Industrial unit wins contract.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Global Industrial Technologies Inc said on Thursday its Harbison-Walker Refractories Co subsidiary won a $25 million contract to supply products for a new coke plant in East Chicago, Ind.</p>
<p>The plant is being built for Sun Coal and Coke by Raytheon Constructors &amp; Engineers, which hired Harbison to supply 73,000 metric tons of premium silica and fireclay-based refractory products.</p>
<p>Sun Coal is a unit of Sun Co Inc. Raytheon Constructors is owned by Raytheon Co.</p>
</text>
